  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    # Initialize result grid with all 3s\n    res = [[3 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    if n <= 1:\n        return res\n    \n    # Start position for the spiral of 0s\n    r, c = 1, 0\n    res[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Directions: right, down, left, up\n    directions = [(0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1), (-1, 0)]\n    dir_idx = 0\n    \n    # Generate spiral path with step lengths:\n    # i=0: n-2, i=1: n-3, i=2: n-3, i=3: n-5, i=4: n-5, i=5: n-7...\n    # General formula for step i (0-indexed):\n    # if i==0: n-2\n    # elif i is odd: n-2-i\n    # elif i is even: n-1-i\n    # Run for n-2 steps total\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        if i == 0:\n            step_len = n - 2\n        elif i % 2 == 1:\n            step_len = n - 2 - i\n        else:\n            step_len = n - 1 - i\n        \n        if step_len <= 0:\n            break\n        \n        dr, dc = directions[dir_idx]\n        for _ in range(step_len):\n            r += dr\n            c += dc\n            if 0 <= r < n and 0 <= c < n:\n                res[r][c] = 0\n        \n        dir_idx = (dir_idx + 1) % 4\n    \n    return res\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    \n    # Initialize result grid with all 3s\n    res = [[3 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    if n <= 1:\n        return res\n    \n    # Start position for the spiral of 0s\n    r, c = 1, 0\n    res[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Directions: right, down, left, up\n    directions = [(0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1), (-1, 0)]\n    dir_idx = 0\n    \n    # Generate spiral path with step lengths:\n    # i=0: n-2, i=1: n-3, i=2: n-3, i=3: n-5, i=4: n-5, i=5: n-7...\n    # General formula for step i (0-indexed):\n    # if i==0: n-2\n    # elif i is odd: n-2-i\n    # elif i is even: n-1-i\n    # Run for n-2 steps total\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        if i == 0:\n            step_len = n - 2\n        elif i % 2 == 1:\n            step_len = n - 2 - i\n        else:\n            step_len = n - 1 - i\n        \n        if step_len <= 0:\n            break\n        \n        dr, dc = directions[dir_idx]\n        for _ in range(step_len):\n            r += dr\n            c += dc\n            if 0 <= r < n and 0 <= c < n:\n                res[r][c] = 0\n        \n        dir_idx = (dir_idx + 1) % 4\n    \n    return res",
